@@ -49,3 +49,27 @@ availability follows the final executor, not the initially offered model.
 Acceptance: isolated real SQLite/artifact restart tests prove one submission, usage and unknown
 fencing, failed usage writes and committed acknowledgement loss; delayed fixture answers prove Stop and policy/tier withdrawal; response fixtures prove
 observed usage survives observer/refresh failure. No hosted inference or visual acceptance is claimed.
+
+Chat decision scores preserve finite values within the zero-based ordered rubric (0 through criteria.length - 1), including fractional
+interpolations such as 1.5, matching the existing classifier transport. Invalid, missing or
+out-of-rubric scores remain errors; offered-label and distribution checks retain their existing policy.
+
+Chat decisions retain the declared ModelUsage counters and actually reported request cost/native
+model identity through post-response failure. Unknown facts remain absent. Both existing usage
+consumers map those counters to the same ledger columns; no account identity or auth kind is inferred.
+A chat decision selects Single through the existing invocation/retry owner: at most one physical
+API attempt, including empty/signature/off-peak branches. Default and Unbounded calls retain their
+existing behavior. Native whole executors gain no retry or permission policy. The original Stop
+signal and total ten-second admission/request deadline remain; failure retains billed facts and
+abstains without a replacement inference.
+
+Existing model-error usage observations are read through the shared facts contract, matched to
+exact provider/model identity and bounded cause traversal; no completed answer is inferred from
+usage alone. The original Core reader re-exports that same function.
+
+Only a chat response ending with `stop` and valid answers may complete a decision. Other finish
+reasons abstain while retaining observed billing facts, including server-tool-only failed receipts.
+
+Choice distributions retain only documented four-decimal rounding tolerance, matching the installed
+classifier rule `max(0.001, labelCount * 0.00005)`. Choice/score confidence must be a reported finite
+value in [0,1]; missing or invalid values fail instead of borrowing the selected probability or zero.
